  "style": {
    "id": "differential-growth",
    "name": "Differential Growth",
    "description": "A bright pastel studio: a coral-pink paper ribbon stands on edge inside a low clear glass hoop on a warm white table in front of a mint sweep. The ribbon keeps growing longer but the hoop does not get bigger, so the ring swells to the glass, buckles into a row of waves that fold inward, each wave sprouts smaller waves, and the hoop ends packed with one continuous, never-crossing ribbon (seen from straight above as a coral maze). The ribbon is a stepped 2D simulation run once at load (springs, bending, short-range repulsion, a circular wall, points inserted as it grows), stored per video frame and extruded upward; a light band can run along its whole length to show it is a single strip.",
